<title>UK: UK cocoa imports rose sharply in January.</title>
<headline>UK cocoa imports rose sharply in January.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>UK cocoa imports in tonnes issued by UK Customs - cocoa beans whole or broken, raw or roasted:</p>
<p>			   JAN     DEC   JAN 1996</p>
<p> TOTAL		35,177  19,115	24,498</p>
<p> Sierra Leone	  989     771	   592</p>
<p> Ivory Coast	 6,376   4,612	 9,857</p>
<p> Ghana		 5,853   1,651	 3,050</p>
<p> Nigeria	    14,852   6,966	 8,070</p>
<p> Cameroon		859     465	   nil</p>
<p> Sao Tome-Principe   nil     nil	   nil</p>
<p> Tanzania		454	99	    99</p>
<p> Mexico		  360     327	   nil</p>
<p> Indonesia	   5,031     245	   nil</p>
<p> Papua New Guinea    400     343	    60</p>
<p> Vanuatu		 nil     nil	   341</p>
<p> Others		  nil   3,636	 2,429</p>
<p>		     Cocoa butter, fat and oil</p>
<p> TOTAL		 1,334   1,352	   696</p>
<p> Turkey		  nil     nil	    60</p>
<p> Ghana		   425     552	   135</p>
<p> Nigeria		 395     220	    22</p>
<p> Indonesia	     160	80	   120</p>
<p> Malaysia		220     260	   120</p>
<p> Others		  134     240	   239</p>
